{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/etbktw","slideIndex":2,"text":"The capacities and base latencies are configurable project assumptions, not course-provided benchmark values. Tasks are processed in fixed order. For projected load, capacity-aware ranks a node by the larger of its post-placement CPU and RAM utilization. Lowest-latency-first ranks by configured latency plus the projected load penalty. Both require sufficient remaining CPU and RAM. QoS targets are explicit assumptions and placement success is reported separately from target success. Evidence: cdefsim/models.py, cdefsim/policies.py, and the README assumptions."}
