{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/6rcqh6","slideIndex":4,"text":"Overload setup: 12 tasks each need 8 CPU and 8 GB RAM; total CPU demand is 96 vs 88 available. Expected at most 11 can be placed, with fallback to another eligible tier and then rejection. Actual both policies placed 11, rejected 1, and used Edge/Fog/Cloud counts 1/2/8. After Edge became ineligible, lowest-latency-first placed 10 elsewhere and capacity-aware placed 2 elsewhere under its ranking. Capacity experiment setup: rerun seed 305, increase only Cloud RAM from 64 to 96 GB. Expected acceptance to improve; latency and QoS may shift. Actual both placed 15/rejected 5, up 3 placed. Mean latency became 49.11 and 49.10 ms. QoS met was 7 for lowest-latency-first and 7 for capacity-aware. Evidence: overload_results.csv, overload_summary.json, overload_trace.csv, capacity_change_comparison.json, capacity_changed_results.csv, capacity_changed_summary.json, all under results/experiments/."}
