{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/fk56h1","slideIndex":5,"text":"VM records are in memory only and account against the same node CPU/RAM pool. Tenant access is an ownership check rather than authentication. The cross-tenant response matches the missing-record response and returns no task contents. The current test suite had 19 passing checks when the report was built. To reproduce, install requirements, run the seeded CLI, run the experiment generator, and run unittest. Limitations should be stated clearly in the viva: this is a deterministic classroom simulation, not a live cloud deployment or benchmark. Evidence: results/experiments/tenant_isolation.json and the test run recorded during report generation."}